From a1da057404097c9a06fad59598906e052bd44ec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:23:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] BananaDS: the Gengis workers wake on a claimable bin
 alone

The workers' wake condition compared the frame number (Gen, written by the emulator's thread outside the mutex)
with the one they last saw, as before the pipeline: a benign data race on a plain unsigned, and not needed, since
a frame's start stores its claim word under the mutex and notifies. The condition is now the claim word alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
---
 bananads/src/gengis_renderer.cpp | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bananads/src/gengis_renderer.cpp b/bananads/src/gengis_renderer.cpp
index d59e6fb..a0cbe5e 100644
--- a/bananads/src/gengis_renderer.cpp
+++ b/bananads/src/gengis_renderer.cpp
@@ -301,13 +301,12 @@ bool GengisRenderer3D::RenderOne(bool emu) {
 }
 
 void GengisRenderer3D::Worker() {
-    unsigned seen = 0;
     for (;;) {
         {
+            // (a frame's start stores its claim word under M and notifies: a bin to claim is the whole condition)
             std::unique_lock<std::mutex> l(M);
-            Wake.wait(l, [&] { return Quit || (Gen != seen && (uint32_t)Claim.load(std::memory_order_acquire) < GX_NBINS); });
+            Wake.wait(l, [&] { return Quit || (uint32_t)Claim.load(std::memory_order_acquire) < GX_NBINS; });
             if (Quit) return;
-            seen = Gen;
         }
         while (RenderOne()) {}
     }
